the first plane load of baby formula  arrived in the u.s from germany today as  the biden administration tries to  resolve a shortage hitting too close to  home for parents all across our country  elise preston has the latest  the u.s military cargo plane carrying 78  thousand pounds of desperately needed  baby formula landed in indianapolis  sunday's operation fly formula flight  from germany was the first of several  expected from europe this week the c-17  brought in 132 pallets of nestle brand  specialty formula it is a large shipment  a very specific and specialized formula  formula for moms and dads who have  children who have allergies where the  regular form formula just simply will  not work the white house is scrambling  to bring relief to parents across the  u.s struggling to find formula the  shortage worsen when the nation's  largest domestic formula manufacturing  plant was shut down in february after a  whistleblower raised safety concerns  federal officials say abbott nutrition's  michigan facility may resume operations  in the coming days but it will take  about two months before product is ready  for delivery at least four babies have  been hospitalized in south carolina  because of complications related to the  shortage these planes that are landing  right now are going to provide some  incremental relief in the coming days  we're going to keep working on it over  the course of weeks and in an effort to  prevent formula price gouging new york  city mayor eric adams declared a state  of emergency on sunday elise preston cbs  news new york
 

